    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n34359" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pĕdo</span></b> , āvi,
			ātum, 1, v. a.
		pes, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to foot</i>, i. e. <i>to furnish with feet;</i>
			hence, * </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> Male
			pedatus, <i>ill set on his feet</i>, <i><span class="en">Suet.
				Oth. 12</span></i>.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>To prop up trees</i> or <i>vines</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vineae pedandae cura,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Col. 4,
					12</span></i>
			.</div>
